{"k":"p","w":10,"r":[{"t":"•In simple terms, Newton’s 3rd law postulates that if object A exerts a force on object B, object B exerts a force (equal in magnitude but opposite in direction) on object A. "},{"t":"Action = Reaction. ~ ","b":1},{"t":"Therefore, all feats presented and calculated "},{"t":"here","u":1,"a":"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17wmc4NAUb3CXdQcSo-XC87joOr-dOqNCkZZDzQDRkl4/edit"},{"t":" would scale for the durability of said characters. Any character bullrushing or striking would also need to withstand the recoil of their own attack."}]},
